<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH SKODA AUTO DETAILS 1996 RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CZECH SKODA AUTO DETAILS 1996 RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech car maker Skoda</p>
<p>Automobilova a.s., a unit of Germany's Volkswagen AG, on</p>
<p>Thursday detailed its audited financial results for 1996.</p>
<p>Results for year ending December 31, 1996: (in millions of</p>
<p>crowns)</p>
<p> Net result		   163 profit vs     1,621 loss</p>
<p> Total sales	     58,898	  vs    43,945</p>
<p> Added value		8,844	  vs     5,751</p>
<p> Personnel costs	  3,820	  vs     2,988</p>
<p> Depreciation	     3,573	  vs     3,604</p>
<p> Total production	59,892	  vs    44,604</p>
<p>Balance of other</p>
<p> income and expenditure  -931	  vs	-558</p>
<p>Result from</p>
<p> financial operations    -357	  vs	-222</p>
<p> Change in inventories    624	  vs	 310</p>
<p>Capitalisation of internally</p>
<p> produced assets	    370	  vs	 349</p>
<p>Material and energy</p>
<p> consumption	     43,782	  vs    32,048</p>
<p>Purchased goods</p>
<p> and services	     7,266	  vs     6,805</p>
<p>Workforce</p>
<p> (No. of employees)    17,992	  vs    16,835</p>
<p> Cash flow		  4,422	  vs     2,785</p>
<p> Investments	     10,680	  vs     5,613</p>
<p>Equity/fixed</p>
<p> assets (pct)	     105.4	  vs	135.6</p>
<p> Equity capital	  26,469	  vs     26,801</p>
<p> Total assets	    42,440	  vs     39,094</p>
<p>Revenue by territory</p>
<p> Czech Rep &amp; Slovakia  26,538	  vs     21,472</p>
<p> Western Europe	  18,077	  vs     12,321</p>
<p>Central and</p>
<p> eastern Europe	  10,393	  vs	5,850</p>
<p> Overseas and Asia	3,890	  vs	4,302</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
